.TH TRAYGOLIN 1 "2026-10-07" "traygolin 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
traygolin \- unofficial Linux tray app for the Pangolin VPN client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B traygolin
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Traygolin is an unofficial GTK4/Libadwaita tray app that drives the official
Pangolin CLI (\fBpangolin\fR). It is not affiliated with Fossorial or Pangolin.
.PP
The header switch connects and disconnects. The sidebar shows this device and
each site the tunnel reaches.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-hide-window
Start in the tray without showing the window.
.TP
.BI \-\-poll-interval " SECONDS"
Override the status refresh interval for this process. Minimum 1.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show GTK application help.
.SH SETTINGS
Schema \fBio.github.lucasssvaz.Traygolin\fR:
.TP
.B poll-interval
Seconds between status checks (default 5).
.TP
.B tray-icon
Show the tray icon (default true).
.TP
.B start-at-login
Install an XDG autostart entry.
.TP
.B connect-at-start
Connect when Traygolin starts.
.TP
.B mtu
WireGuard MTU passed to \fBpangolin up\fR.
.TP
.B holepunch
Enable NAT holepunching on connect.
.TP
.B disable-relay
Do not fall back to relaying.
.SH PRIVILEGES
The Pangolin CLI starts its tunnel through \fBsudo\fR. When run by Traygolin,
that call reaches Traygolin, which validates it and runs
\fI/usr/lib/traygolin/traygolin-helper\fR through \fBpkexec\fR(1). The polkit
action \fBio.github.lucasssvaz.Traygolin.tunnel\fR allows the active local user to do
this without a password.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/run/olm.sock
Local control socket of the running tunnel.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pangolin/config.json
Pangolin CLI configuration (DNS and routing preferences).
.TP
.I ~/.config/pangolin/accounts.json
Saved CLI accounts. Traygolin never copies the secrets in this file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pangolin/logs/client.log
Client log shown in View Logs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.lucasssvaz.Traygolin.desktop
Written when Start at Login is enabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR polkit (8)
.PP
Documentation in the source tree under \fIdocs/\fR.
